[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"MongoDB Aggregation Operators: A Comprehensive Guide"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"MongoDB's aggregation framework provides powerful tools for data processing and transformation. Aggregation operators are the building blocks of aggregation pipelines, allowing you to perform calculations, manipulate strings, work with arrays, and handle dates. This tutorial explores various aggregation operators categorized by their function: Arithmetic, String, Array, and Date."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Arithmetic Operators"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Arithmetic operators perform mathematical calculations on numeric values. Common operators include $add, $subtract, $multiply, $divide, and $mod."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"// Example: Calculating total price with tax
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      orderId: 1,
      totalPrice: {
        $add: [ "$price", {
          $multiply: ["$price", 0.07] // 7% tax
        }]
      }
    }
  }
])"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"In the example above, the '$add' operator calculates the total price by adding the original price to the tax amount, which is calculated using the '$multiply' operator."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"String Operators"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"String operators allow you to manipulate string values. Key operators include $concat, $substr, $toLower, $toUpper, and $strLenBytes."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"// Example: Concatenating first and last names
db.users.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      fullName: {
        $concat: ["$firstName", " ", "$lastName"]
      }
    }
  }
])"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example uses the '$concat' operator to combine the 'firstName' and 'lastName' fields into a single 'fullName' field."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Array Operators"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Array operators enable you to work with arrays within your documents. Important operators include $size, $slice, $filter, and $unwind."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"// Example: Getting the size of an array
db.products.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      name: 1,
      numCategories: { $size: "$categories" }
    }
  }
])"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$size' operator returns the number of elements in the 'categories' array."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"// Example: Unwinding an array
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $unwind: "$items"
  },
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      orderId: 1,
      itemName: "$items.name",
      itemQuantity: "$items.quantity"
    }
  }
])"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$unwind' operator deconstructs the 'items' array, creating a new document for each element in the array."},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Date Operators"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Date operators allow you to extract and manipulate date values. Useful operators include $year, $month, $dayOfMonth, $hour, and $dateToString."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"// Example: Extracting the year from a date
db.events.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      eventName: 1,
      eventYear: { $year: "$eventDate" }
    }
  }
])"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$year' operator extracts the year from the 'eventDate' field."},{"order":21,"type":"code","text":"// Example: Formatting a date as a string
db.events.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      eventName: 1,
      formattedDate: {
        $dateToString: {
          format: "%Y-%m-%d",
          date: "$eventDate"
        }
      }
    }
  }
])"},{"order":22,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$dateToString' operator formats the 'eventDate' field into a string with the specified format."},{"order":23,"type":"paragraph","text":"By combining these aggregation operators, you can create complex pipelines to transform and analyze your data effectively in MongoDB."}]
